---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import hackpad from "../../../assets/hackpad.jpg";
---

<Layout>
    <a href="/projects/" class="backToBtn">Back to Projects</a>

    <div class="projectPage">
        <h1>Hackpad</h1>
        <img
            src={hackpad.src}
            alt="Cool ass four key keyboard"
            class="largeProjectImg"
        />
        <p>
            After taking a long break from Blueprint and getting an actually
            good laptop, I decided to give Kicad a try. I had wanted to try it
            with my friend but they never had free time. After so much begging
            good laptop, I decided to give Kicad a try. I had wanted to try it
            with my friend but they never had free time. and asking, I gave up
            and decided to make it myself. It took me a couple of days but
            evenually I had a schematic and PCB I was happy with... untill I
            submitted it for review...<br /><br />

            A bit of backstory here. The Blueprint guides sucked. No offence to
            anyone who spent time making them but they were full of
            misinformation and mistakes. I was constantly asking on the Slack
            for help.
            <br />
            <br />
            After submitting 5 times and getting rejected for small problems with
            my Github I submitted one last time and it got approved!! <strong
                >JK</strong
            >, it would never be that easy. Turns out my schematic was extremely
            wrong and it took this long for people getting paid to look at my
            project to realise...
            <br /><br />
            After about another week I had completely remade the schematic and it
            actually got approved this time! Then I built the it and submitted it
            for build review, expecting it to take around a week. Three months later
            it's still in build review...
            <br /><br />
            <strong>Update!!!</strong><br />
            I didn't journal any of it cause the guide has a huge banner on it saying
            "JOURNALLING NOT REQUIRED!" Turns out journalling is required for it so
            it's been rejected. Their loss though, the project doesn't get count as
            shipped untill it's build accepted, therefore Blueprint lost like $15
            bucks on this.
        </p>
        <br />
        <h4>Programs and Links:</h4><br /><br />
        <a
            href="https://blueprint.hackclub.com/projects/9821"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Blueprint!</a
        >
        <a
            href="https://github.com/PL00T00/SpeedrunPad-"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Github!</a
        >
    </div>
    <br /><br /><br />
</Layout>
